---
title: Canvas
description: The Muse board — objects on an infinite pegboard grid, with pan, zoom, and spatial arrangement.
---

The canvas is an infinite, pannable surface. Objects — text, drawings, images, and embeds —
are placed at absolute coordinates and snap to a shared **pegboard** grid so layouts stay
tidy without manual alignment.

## Objects

Every item on a board is an object with a position, size, and type. Objects are themed to
match the active appearance, so a board reads the same in light and dark mode.

| Type      | Description                                  |
| --------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `text`    | Rich text block, edited inline.              |
| `draw`    | Freehand strokes from the draw tool.         |
| `image`   | An uploaded, end-to-end encrypted media blob.|
| `embed`   | A linked card to another board or app.       |

## Pan & zoom

Scroll to pan, pinch or `⌘`-scroll to zoom. The grid scales with the zoom level so the
pegboard spacing stays visually consistent at any distance.

